1) Interviewer asked what is delta lake and parquet?
parquet is a excellent columnar file format with extension as .parquet that gives faster reads and compression.
parquet is a immutable means we can read or write thats it we cant modify the existing data like (updates or deletes)
This was intentional for performance, parallel processing and cloud storage compatibility.
But immutability created serious problems - updates required full file rewrites, deletes not allowed, failed jobs left 
partial data and concurrent writes caused corruption.

* Delta lake brilliantly solved this withpout fighting parquets immutability. Instead of modifying parquet files, delta
lake adds a tranaction_log alongside them.
when you update a row - delta reads the parquet, writes a brand new parquet file with the change, and logs remove old file, 
add new file' in the transaction log. Th old parquet file still physically exits in s3 but is logically invisible to queries.
This approach gives us three things for free -
ACID tranactions because writes are atomic commits to the log, timetravel because old parquet files are preserved until vaccum
deletes them, and rollback because uncommitted transactions are simply never recorded in the log.

