PART 3 — AUTO OPTIMIZE ⚙️
What is Auto Optimize?
"Auto Optimize is Databricks feature that automatically runs optimization in background during write operations — so you don't need to manually run OPTIMIZE!"
Two Components of Auto Optimize:
Auto Optimize = 
    1. Optimized Write      +     2. Auto Compact
    (during write itself)         (after write completes)
Component 1 — Optimized Write
"Before writing data, Databricks automatically shuffles and reorganizes data to produce right-sized parquet files"
WITHOUT Optimized Write:
Your pipeline writes 10GB data in 200 tasks
→ 200 parquet files × 50MB each
→ Some files 5MB, some 200MB (uneven sizes!)
→ Small files problem begins!

WITH Optimized Write:
Your pipeline writes 10GB data in 200 tasks
→ Databricks automatically decides:
  "10GB needs approximately 20 files of 512MB each"
→ Reshuffles data before writing
→ Produces 20 well-sized parquet files!
→ No small files from the start! ✅
Component 2 — Auto Compact
"After write completes, Databricks checks if small files exist and automatically compacts them in background"
WITHOUT Auto Compact:
Write 1 → 50 small files
Write 2 → 50 small files
Write 3 → 50 small files
= 150 small files accumulating!
You must manually run OPTIMIZE!

WITH Auto Compact:
Write 1 → 50 small files
         → Auto Compact runs in background
         → Compacts to 5 larger files ✅
Write 2 → few small files
         → Auto Compact runs again ✅
Write 3 → few small files
         → Auto Compact runs again ✅
= Always optimized! No manual work!
How to Enable Auto Optimize
Method 1 — For Specific Table
-- Enable both components for a table
ALTER TABLE employees
SET TBLPROPERTIES (
  'delta.autoOptimize.optimizeWrite' = 'true',
  'delta.autoOptimize.autoCompact'   = 'true'
);

-- Disable if needed
ALTER TABLE employees
SET TBLPROPERTIES (
  'delta.autoOptimize.optimizeWrite' = 'false',
  'delta.autoOptimize.autoCompact'   = 'false'
);
Method 2 — For Entire Spark Session
# Enable for all tables in this session
spark.conf.set("spark.databricks.delta/.optimizeWrite.enabled", "true")
spark.conf.set("spark.databricks.delta/.autoCompact.enabled", "true")
Method 3 — While Creating Table
CREATE TABLE employees (
  emp_id INT,
  name STRING,
  salary INT,
  department STRING
)
USING DELTA
TBLPROPERTIES (
  'delta.autoOptimize.optimizeWrite' = 'true',
  'delta.autoOptimize.autoCompact'   = 'true'
);
When to Use Auto Optimize?
Enable Auto Optimize for:
✅ Streaming tables          (writes every few seconds/minutes)
✅ Frequently appended tables (daily batch loads)
✅ Tables used for reporting  (always need fast queries)
✅ Tables with ad-hoc writes  (unpredictable write patterns)

Be careful with Auto Optimize for:
⚠️ Very large tables (100TB+) — compaction overhead is high
⚠️ Tables with very heavy write SLAs
   (optimized write adds slight latency to each write)
⚠️ Temporary/staging tables  (no need to optimize throwaway data)

