Difference between standard Execution engine (spark jvm) vs Photon Engine?
Standard Engine (Spark JVM) = Old Ambassador car (old technology, slow speed, more fuel consumption)
Photon Engine (C++) = Modern Formula f1 car (latest technology, high speed, fuel efficient)

standard engine means it is Apache spark defaults query execution engine - it runs on (Java Virual Machine JVM)
JVM works - convert our query into java byte code - JVM interpret - then send instructions to cpu - then result
For getting results it needs to follow extra steps it consumes more time to get result.
problems with JVM
- Garbage collection
- Row by Row processing
- Memory Overhead

Photon Engine - It was released by databricks in 2021,It was written in native C++ query execution engine - This intracts directly with
CPU (no need JVM steps) so processing very fast.

Photon engine secret powers:
power1 - Vectorized processing (standard - row by row for each,    photon - set of multiple rows )
power2 - CPU SIMD Instructions (single instruction multiple data)
power3 - No garbage collection
power4 - Better memory management

Standard spark execution engine runs on JVM. it processes data row by row, suffers from garbage collection pauses, and
has significant memory overhead. for analytical queries this becomes slow and expensive

Photon is databricks own query engine written in C++, It bypasses JVM completely and talks directly to the cpu. 
It uses vectorized processing - meaning it processes thousands of rows in a single batch instead of one by one. It also
useS CPU SMID instructions for parallel calculations and has zero garbage collection pauses.

Result - Same sql query on same data runs 3 to 5 times faster on photon. It is automatically enabled on sql warehouses
and optionally available on clusters. For BI and analytical workloads, photon dramatically improves performance and reduces
cost because queries finish faster meaning cluster runs for less time.

