Spark cache vs delta cache?
spark cache - stores RDD/DATAFRAME data in JVM memory or disk across cluster nodes.
purpose - reuse same dataframe multiple times in same spark session without recomputing
df.cache() - memory only, df.persist() - memory + disk, df.unpersist() - remove cache
key points : 
lives in JVM memory
lost when cluster restarts or session ends
you manually control what to cache
works for any data - delta, parquet, csv, anything ( Any format of data)
storag location - JVM heap memory
good for interative ML algorithms using same data repeatedly


Delta cache - Automatically caches recently accessed parquet/delta files on worker node's local SSD disk.
purpose - Avoid repeatedly reading same files from remote cloud storage(s3/adls) by keeping them locally on worker nodes
key points:
Lives on local SSD of worker nodes
Automatic - no code needed
persists across spark sessions and cluster restarts
only works for delta lake and parquet files
Enabled by default on certain databricks instance types

when to use what?
use spark cache when 
same dataframe used multiple times in your code
complex transformations you dont want to repeat
iterative ML training loops

use delta cache when
same delta tables queried repeatedly by analysis
BI dashboards hitting same tables multiple times
want faster reads without changing any code

