TEMP VIEW VS GLOBAL TEMP VIEW?
TEMP view - A virtual table created from a dataframe - visible only within same SPARKSESSION
write SQL on top of a dataframe within your current notebook
df.createOrReplaceTempView("sales_view")
spark.sql("select * from sales_view")

Keypoints :
Lives only in current notebook session
Dies when sparksession ends or notebook detaches
not visible to other notebooks
no database prefix needed - just use name directly

GLOBAL TEMP VIEW?
A virtual table visible across multiple notebooks on same cluster
share a view between different notebooks without saving as a delta table
df.createOrReplaceGlobalTempView("sales_global")
spark.sql("select * from global_temp.sales_global")

Key points:
Lives as long as cluster is running
dies when cluster restarts
visible to all notebooks attached to same cluster
must use global_temp.prefix always
slightly more overhead than temp view

